Why no candidate ever reaches its personality's probe()

The panel of run 552 ends with Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6 and nothing after it.
Q is written once per entry into probeCandidates, so the matching entered it
six times.  P1, which is written right before inst->probe(), never appears:
no candidate was ever probed, so no personality was loaded, so IOBSD never
appeared, and bsd_init waits for a root device that will not come.

The reasons are already recorded -- NIO_DROP writes down why each candidate
was turned away, and the summary at the end of probeCandidates prints them.
But that summary goes through printf, into the console ring, and the ring is
where the boot went silent: the run 546 panel showed the matching's marks
and none of bsd_init's phases for exactly that reason.  So the reasons are
written to the panel as well, where they cannot be lost.

The numbers are the reasons, in the order the candidates were offered:

  1  the candidate is a dext and dexts are off
  2  a dext relaunch is needed and the budget is spent
  3  the match category was consumed by another client
  4  the properties could not be copied
  5  the nub does not match the personality
  6  the kext that holds the personality is not loaded
  7  the client is being terminated for replacement
  8  the match category was consumed
  9  the personality is not the one being rematched

Reason 6 is the one that matters: the kext is not in the kernel, so the
matching waits for a module that will never be loaded, and every candidate
that needs it is turned away.  K says which class was asked for.

R is the reason, K the class of the personality, and the summary at the end
repeats them as "nio: S <provider> r=<reasons> n=<class>".

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
index 23b8d83..bd01596 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOService.cpp
@@ -4058,6 +4058,16 @@ nio_reason_rank(int reason)
 			nio_class_name(match, nio_best_name, 24); \
 		} \
 		nio_nreasons++; \
+		/* nio: the same reason on the panel.  The console is where the boot \
+		 * went silent, so the summary below never arrived on the screen; \
+		 * the reasons are what say which door the candidates were turned \
+		 * away at.  R is the reason, K the class of the personality. */ \
+		char nio_drop_name[24]; \
+		nio_class_name(match, nio_drop_name, 24); \
+		nio_u_mark("\nR"); \
+		nio_uhex((unsigned long)(n)); \
+		nio_u_mark("\nK"); \
+		nio_u_mark(nio_drop_name); \
 	} \
 } while (0)
 
@@ -4462,6 +4472,12 @@ IOService::probeCandidates( OSOrderedSet * matches )
 		}
 		printf("\nnio: S %s r=%s n=%s", getName() ? getName() : "?", nio_buf,
 		    nio_best_name[0] ? nio_best_name : "?");
+		nio_u_mark("\nnio: S ");
+		nio_u_mark(getName() ? getName() : "?");
+		nio_u_mark("\nr=");
+		nio_u_mark(nio_buf);
+		nio_u_mark("\nn=");
+		nio_u_mark(nio_best_name[0] ? nio_best_name : "?");
 	}
 
 	OSSafeReleaseNULL(matches);
